        "original_id": "9d5840a4-7f25-5dce-986c-e0850496afb6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Cyril Briggs\n- Organizations: The Crusader, African Blood Brotherhood\n- Concepts: Pan-Africanism, New Negro Movement\n\nFacts:\n- Cyril Briggs is best remembered as the founder and editor of The Crusader, a seminal New York magazine of the New Negro Movement of the 1920s.\n- Cyril Briggs is also remembered as the founder of the African Blood Brotherhood, a small but historically important radical organization.\n- The African Blood Brotherhood was dedicated to advancing the cause of Pan-Africanism.\n- Pan-Africanism is a worldwide intellectual movement that aims to encourage and strengthen bonds of solidarity among all people of African descent.",
